## Scenario — what attendees are told at kickoff (read this aloud)

> It's **14:10 on an ordinary Tuesday**. Customers start reporting that the Normain web app is throwing errors and the API is returning 500s. On-call checks the dashboards: the **primary production database on Azure is unreachable and core tables appear to be missing**. The customer-facing product is effectively **down**.
>
> You've just been paged. Work through what we do — from this moment to full recovery and the all-clear.

That's all the participants know. They see the surface; they do not know the cause.

---

## Facilitator ground truth — DO NOT read aloud (you hold the whole truth)

- **Root cause:** at **14:02** an engineer ran a data-migration script against **production instead of staging**, truncating core tables in the production PostgreSQL database (Azure). **Human error — not malicious, not a breach, no data exfiltration.**
- **Backups:** automated nightly backup completed at **02:00 today** on Azure. Last good backup is **~12h old** → **within the 24h RPO**. Restoring it loses ~12h of transactions (acceptable per RPO, but must be reconciled).
- **Mapping (Appendix B, Rank 1 "Hosting facility / Product down"):** **RTO 12h, RPO 24h**, owner **Engineering**. Recovery must complete inside 12h to meet the plan.
- **Reality of recovery:** restoring from the 02:00 backup to a fresh instance + verification is realistically ~3–4h. So the team *can* meet RTO if they act — the exercise is about whether they know how.

### True timeline (reveal only through questioning/injects)
- 14:02 — migration script run against prod
- 14:05 — background errors begin
- 14:10 — customer reports + on-call paged ← **exercise starts here**
- (everything after this is what the team should work out)

